<div class="page">
  <h1 style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 30px;">Instructions for Preparing Form W-2</h1>
  <p>The 6-part wage and tax statement is acceptable in most States. If you are in doubt, ask your appropriate State or local official.</p>
  <p>Prepare Form W-2 for each of your employees to whom any of the following items applied during 1979:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>(a) You withheld income tax or FICA (social security)</li>
    <li>(b) You would have withheld income tax if the employee had not claimed more than one withholding allowance.</li>
    <li>(c) You paid $600 or more.</li>
    <li>(d) You paid for services any amount, if you are in a trade or business.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>By January 31, 1980, give Copies B, C, and 2 to each person who was your employee at the end of 1979. For anyone who stopped working for you before the end of 1979, you should give copies within 30 days after the last wage payment. Send Copy A to the Social Security Administration by February 29, 1980. (For more information, please see Forms 941, 942, W-3, or Circular E. Farmers, see Circular A.)</p>
  <p>See separate Instructions for Forms W-2 and W-2P for more information on how to complete Form W-2.</p>
</div>

